From cc19340feb34345bb28d7fb380209609c8cb2f65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Kang <allen.kang@mitaccomputing.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 08:29:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: mic-cpld-4826: fix tach mapping and RPM conversion

The second CPLD tach register bank starts at 0x21, but hwmon exposes
it as channels 16 through 31. Adding the hwmon channel directly to
0x21 accesses registers 0x31 through 0x40 instead of 0x21 through
0x30.

Translate the second-bank channel to a zero-based index before
forming the register address. The CPLD tach value represents
380 RPM per count, so replace the incorrect factor of 40 with a
named RPM conversion constant.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [No upstream maintenance]
---
 drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.c | 2 +-
 drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.h | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.c b/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.c
index 5ca4352e2b05..b05499e48dbd 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.c
@@ -277,7 +277,7 @@ static int mic_cpld_4826_read(struct device *dev, enum hwmon_sensor_types type,
 			if (ret < 0)
 				return ret;
 
-			*val = ret * 40;
+			*val = ret * TACH_RPM_PER_COUNT;
 			return 0;
 		}
 		break;
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.h b/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.h
index 052fa44d38e4..2df8803acd9d 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.h
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/mic-cpld-4826.h
@@ -5,7 +5,9 @@
 
 #define REG_PWM(ch) (0x31 + (ch))
 #define REG_TACH_1(ch) (0x11 + (ch))
-#define REG_TACH_2(ch) (0x21 + (ch))
+/* Map hwmon channels 16..31 (fan17..fan32) to tach registers 0x21..0x30. */
+#define REG_TACH_2(ch) (0x21 + ((ch) - 16))
+#define TACH_RPM_PER_COUNT 380
 #define REG_LEAKAGE 0x08
 
 #define MAX_PWM_CHANNELS 16
-- 
2.34.1

